W9 LIBTAM 0.10.0 (TAM-EDIT 1.1.1)

Date: 2026-11-26
AI harness: Claude Code 2.1.332
AI model: claude-opus-5-5


GUIDANCE

  Fred: "do 0.10.0" (libtam's 0.7 refactor, P1 0.10.0: fix the core
  semantics and migrate every caller in the same slice).


DONE

  - Builds against libtam 0.10.0: tam_fs_read replaces tam_fs_read_file,
    and tam_fs_write_atomic takes flags.
  - Saving keeps the file's permissions (TAM_FS_KEEP_MODE) and writes
    through a symbolic link to its target. Before, every save forced
    0644: scripts lost +x, 0600 files became world-readable, and a
    symlink became a plain file. New files are still 0644. Covered by
    test_save_keeps_mode_and_link.
  - Opening a FIFO, device or directory now fails at once instead of
    hanging (tam_fs_read).
  - Makefile: requires libtam 0.10.0, relinks when libtam.a changes, and
    rebuilds main.o and render.o when VERSION changes (the footer
    showed the old version after a bump).
  - make test passes.


FAILED

  - Nothing.


HANDOFF

  - Next libtam slices (0.11.0, 0.12.0) bring tty suspend/restore,
    paste and mouse events, key names and base64, which replace
    tam-edit's own copies (libtam plans/P1).
